    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Jacob Wilson** (71.05) headline our starting lineup as the premier efficiency plays. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a massive 14% boost due to a favorable platoon matchup against Yesavage, while **Jacob Wilson** is primed for a high-impact game leading off against Patrick Sandoval; his combination of a strong park factor and top-of-the-order positioning makes him a plug-and-play staple. **Heliot Ramos** (67.19) also warrants attention as a high-upside play, bolstered by a 6.00 xERA opposing starter and a favorable wind direction that should help his power profile against the lefty Pannone.\n\nWhile we are deep in talent, the most difficult decision today was leaving **Gunnar Henderson** (45.90) on the bench. Despite his pedigree, the matchup against an elite arm in Skubal (2.62 xERA) coupled with a sharp negative platoon adjustment forced him below our current threshold. He fell just short of the efficiency baseline established by **Sam Antonacci**, whose leadoff role and platoon advantage created a higher daily probability for production. We are also monitoring a 45% rain risk for **Drake Baldwin** and **Luis Robert Jr.**; should weather force a delay or cancellation, we will need to re-evaluate our position, particularly for **Luis Robert Jr.**, who is already contending with a difficult matchup against Sale.\n\nFinally, we are leaning into speed and volume today, evidenced by the start of **Andy Pages** (58.00). His projection is buoyed by an 87% stolen base success rate metric against the opposing starter's delivery, which aligns perfectly with our organizational priority of hunting for scarce stolen bases. **Kyle Tucker** (59.68) remains in the mix despite a neutral lineup projection, as his raw talent floor stays well above our bench options like **Coby Mayo** or **Wade Meckler**, ensuring that our total offensive footprint remains consistent even in tougher individual matchups.",
